 5. 💵 Trump&#x27;s Fed fury 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Via Truth Social 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Fed's decision to raise interest rates yesterday for the first time in three years put new Fed chairman Kevin Warsh immediately at odds with the man who picked him, Axios' Neil Irwin and Rebecca Falconer write. 

 The Fed unanimously raised rates a quarter point, to between 3.75% and 4%. Twelve of 18 officials expect another hike this year, while four expect two more. President Trump responded on Truth Social : "LOWER THE INTEREST RATES FOR THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA, AND FAST!" He said rates should be 1% or lower. Later, Trump said he still has confidence in Warsh while blaming the rest of the Fed for the hike: "I'm relying on Kevin, but he's got a very tough board."

