 6. ⚡ Scoop: Trump plans Gulf summit on Iran 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump attends a campaign rally for Republican Senate hopeful Michael Whatley yesterday in Gastonia, N.C. Photo: Matt Kelley/AP President Trump is expected to hold a meeting with Gulf leaders on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York on Tuesday to discuss the next steps in the war with Iran, Axios' Barak Ravid scoops. 

 Why it matters: The meeting is expected to focus on U.S. ideas for a postwar strategy as Trump and his senior team work on a day-after plan expected to be finalized after the midterms. The sources said Trump will meet with leaders or foreign ministers from the Gulf Cooperation Council countries — Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait and Oman. 

