 8. 🍻 1 fun thing: America&#x27;s Oktoberfest capital 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A man wears souvenir pins on his alpine hat during Oktoberfest Zinzinnati in 2021. Photo: Jeff Dean/AFP via Getty Images The world's largest Oktoberfest celebration outside Munich takes place in ... Cincinnati.

 Oktoberfest Zinzinnati , which started as a street festival in 1976, drew a record 808,300 people last year. It turns 50 when it starts today, Axios Cincinnati's Kristen Swilley writes. By the numbers: At a recent Oktoberfest, attendees consumed:

 🌭 87,542 metts (a German sausage). 🥨 23,004 soft pretzels. 🍰 20,000 cream puffs. 🥬 3,600 pounds of sauerkraut. 🧀 702 pounds of Limburger cheese. More on Zinzinnati ... Get Axios Local : Newsletters in 43 cities. 

 
 
